  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "CMake: Also make the stack 8MiB on non-MSVC Windows builds",
  "description": "On Windows, the main thread stack maximum (reserve) stack size for an\nexecutable is set in the PE header.[1] The default value for ARM64, x86,\nand x64 machines is 1MiB.[2]\n\nThe default on Linux and macOS is 8MiB. We use a linker option with MSVC\nto increase the size on Windows to 8MiB as well.\n(see commit 086f4f1133e5b0b7a7172f5dff847d2bfc487461)\n\nAdd the appropriate link option when using non-MSVC compilers if the\nlinker supports it, as GNU ld does on MingW, etc.\n\n[1] https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/debug/pe-format#optional-header-windows-specific-fields-image-only\n\n[2] https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/build/reference/stack-stack-allocations?view=msvc-170\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
